  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The following reaction proceeds through Anti-Markownikoff's addition. Boron gets attached to the more substituted Carbon and the acidic Deuterium from <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>COOD</mtext></mrow></math> gets attached to the less substituted Carbon.<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image71-0b259627-401d-4bfa-97ea-049ceb18115e.jpg\" />",
